DATE DATA TYPES:
TIMESTAMP:
❖	Like DATE but adds fractions of seconds (date + time + fractional seconds - up to 9 digits).
❖	Useful when recording events (e.g., log records).
SYNTAX: TIMESTAMP [(fractional_seconds_precision)]
Default precision is 6.
Real-world use case:
❖	Logging when a transaction happened, e.g. ATM withdrawal at 2025-09-04 12:34:56.789123.
❖	Storing high-frequency sensor data (IoT, stock trades, etc.)
